on, each new test goes red for exactly its branch and green again on revert:\n- delete the _is_at_level call in _same_level_neighbors -> test_check_cycle_at_level_refuses_a_target_at_another_level fails (verdict flips False -> True).\n- delete the state-is-None + tombstone stub branch -> test_unreducible_dir_with_a_tombstone_yields_a_status_only_stub fails ([] -> ['tkt-target']).\n- delete the state['status'] = tombstone_status override -> test_tombstone_status_overrides_the_reduced_status fails (['tkt-target'] -> []).\n- make _read_tombstone_status's except return None -> test_malformed_tombstone_degrades_to_deleted_not_to_absent fails (['tkt-target'] -> []).\n\nTwo findings worth recording, neither a defect:\n1. The two level guards in _same_level_neighbors are NOT interchangeable. An epic -> task -> epic hop is already refused by the inline current-side ticket_type check, so it stays False even with _is_at_level deleted. Only a DIRECT cross-level edge whose far end is source_id is sensitive to the target-side guard. The hop test is kept as an end-to-end pin but it is the direct test that covers the guard.\n2. The reduce-returns-None + tombstone stub is observable through detect_newly_unblocked ONLY when the recorded status is non-terminal. With a terminal status the stub and 'no entry at all' are indistinguishable, because _is_closed_after_batch treats a missing dir as closed. The test therefore uses a tombstone recording 'open' and pins that _read_tombstone_status propagates .get('status', 'deleted') verbatim with no validation. Real tombstones written by rebar delete always record 'deleted'.\n\nNo defect found, so no discovered_from bug filed. Local gates green: all check_* scripts, complexity baseline, make lint, make typecheck, make config-check, the four doc generators produce no diff, and the CI suite (not integration and not external, -n 3) is 12730 passed / 60 skipped. Two errors in that run were the HEAD-movement guard firing because the commit landed mid-run; re-running those two files against a stable HEAD gives 49 passed.","timestamp":1786618927776494001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"STAND-DOWN STATE (peak-window pause, 5-11am PT). Code is LANDED; the ticket close is the only step left.\n\nLanded: Gerrit change 1725, LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1, submitted and MERGED as ec6ea55f0c on main (rebased server-side from local 33d2566334). Tests-only, +181 lines, no src/rebar change. Worktree /Users/joeoakhart/marabou-coverage is realigned to that merged tip.\n\nAll seven acceptance criteria are met and are now ticked.\n\nINCIDENT — this ticket's description was briefly corrupted by me, now REPAIRED. I staged the plan text at the shared path /tmp/desc.md; a parallel agent working ticket deceitful-flannel-jerboa (the plan-review recall-ratchet work) used the same path, and my last 'rebar edit --description' therefore wrote THEIR plan into THIS ticket (EDIT event 1786621446985753001). That is what made the first close attempt fail: the completion verifier was checking their acceptance criterion about 'rebar review-plan outrageous-uncultured-wildebeast', which has nothing to do with this ticket. Only this ticket was affected — I read their file, I did not write to their ticket, and their store record is untouched. Repaired by recovering the correct description verbatim from EDIT event 1786615750316610001 and re-applying it with the checkboxes ticked; the description is back to its reviewed 7151-char text and contains no wildebeast/recall content. Staging now uses a ticket-scoped path, /tmp/marabou-defc/desc.md.\n\nREMAINING WORK AT RESUME (both are LLM ops, deliberately not run during the pause):\n1. REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1 rebar review-plan standard-hyperbolic-marabou. A fresh attestation is needed because the last PASS was earned against the corrupted text; the restore reverted the material and made it stale. Ticking checkboxes is attestation-safe and is NOT the reason.\n2. REBAR_LLM_BEDROCK_REGION=us-east-1 rebar transition standard-hyperbolic-marabou in_progress closed, from this worktree so the merged commit carrying the rebar-ticket trailer is reachable from HEAD.\n\nNo further pushes or submits are needed; nothing is in flight.","timestamp":1786622332863285001}],"created_at":1786602715615909001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"6e90f20e-52e3-4bab-9b68-259610a1d577","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"985c-32d2-e828-4e6a"},{"link_uuid":"7b928bcd-049a-4f01-9c3d-e63f4a6f7366","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"1841-d46c-87e4-4433"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe graph loader/BFS centralization (985c-32d2-e828-4e6a, Gerrit 1708, merged 1c3e945cb8)\nnamed two behaviours as explicit helpers that had previously been inline, and the rebar\ncode-review bot flagged both as untested. The gaps are PRE-EXISTING — the same logic was\nuncovered while inline — but naming them made them visible. Nothing regresses today; the\nrisk is that a future traversal or loader refactor silently drops either behaviour with the\nsuite still green.\n\n## Approach\n\nCharacterization tests ONLY — no `src/rebar` change. Follow the pattern of\n`test_get_all_blocked_by_accumulates_targets_without_a_ticket_dir` (added by 985c in\n`tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py`): assert the behaviour that exists today so the\ntests pin the contract rather than propose a new one. Each new test was validated by\nmutating the production branch locally, observing the test go red, and reverting — the\nmutation results are recorded per criterion below.\n\n### Gap 1 — the cross-level traversal refusal (`rebar.graph._graph`)\n\n`_same_level_neighbors` confines the walk with two separate guards. The CURRENT-side guard is\nan inline `state.get(\"ticket_type\", \"\").lower() != level` early-return on the node being\nexpanded (`_graph.py` L251). The TARGET-side guard is the single call to `_is_at_level`, on\neach candidate dep (`if target and target not in visited and _is_at_level(...)`, L257). Every\nexisting `check_cycle_at_level` test in `test_graph_cycles.py` uses a single uniform level, so\nthe target-side guard is never exercised.\n\nThe two guards are not interchangeable, and this dictates the test shape: for an\n`epic → task → epic` chain the inline CURRENT-side guard alone already stops the walk, so\ndeleting the `_is_at_level` call leaves that case still returning False. The only mutation-sensitive\nprobe is a DIRECT cross-level edge whose far end IS the queried `source_id`:\n`check_cycle_at_level(\"task-M\", \"epic-B\", level=\"epic\")` where `epic-B depends_on task-M`.\nToday `bfs` (in `rebar.graph._relations`) accumulates nothing, so the answer is False;\nwith the target-side `_is_at_level` deleted, `task-M` is yielded and accumulated and the\nanswer flips to True. Both shapes get a test: the direct one pins the guard, the\n`epic → task → epic` hop one pins the end-to-end \"a lower-level hop cannot reconnect two\nsame-level nodes\" contract.\n\n### Gap 2 — the three tombstone-loader branches (`rebar.graph._unblock`)\n\nAll three are driven through the public `detect_newly_unblocked`, not the private\n`_load_states_with_tombstones`. One shared fixture shape makes each branch observable: a\ntarget ticket carrying two `depends_on` LINK events (so the blocking edges live in the\nTARGET's dir and survive an unreducible blocker dir), one blocker closed by the batch and one\nblocker tombstoned. `_was_already_unblocked` then cannot short-circuit, so the verdict turns\nentirely on how the tombstoned blocker's status is loaded.\n\n- (a) reduce-returns-None + tombstone present yields a status-only stub. Observable only when\n  the recorded status is NON-terminal: with the stub the blocker reads `open` and the target\n  is NOT newly unblocked; without it the blocker is absent and\n  `_is_closed_after_batch`'s \"missing dir → tombstoned, treat as closed\" fallback unblocks\n  the target. The test therefore uses a tombstone recording `open` — `_read_tombstone_status`\n  takes `.get(\"status\", \"deleted\")` verbatim with no validation, and that verbatim\n  propagation is exactly what the test pins.\n- (b) a present tombstone's status OVERRIDES the reduced status: an `open` blocker dir with a\n  `{\"status\": \"deleted\"}` tombstone (the payload `rebar._commands.delete` writes) counts as\n  closed and unblocks the target.\n- (c) a malformed tombstone degrades to `deleted` rather than to \"no tombstone\": the same\n  `open` blocker dir with unparseable tombstone bytes still counts as closed.\n\n## Scope\n\n- `tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py` — two tests for the level-confined traversal,\n  reusing the existing `_helpers._make_ticket` / `_write_link_event` / `_get_check_cycle_at_level`.\n- `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py` — three tests, reusing the file's existing\n  `_write_ticket` and `_write_depends_on_link` helpers. No new helper: `_write_ticket(deps=...)`\n  is unusable here because it writes `blocks` links into the BLOCKER's dir, which an\n  unreducible blocker dir cannot carry, but `_write_depends_on_link` already writes the LINK\n  into the DEPENDENT's dir — exactly the shape these fixtures need.\n\nNo file under `src/rebar` is modified. If a test reveals a real defect, it is recorded and\nfiled as a `discovered_from` bug rather than fixed here.\n\n## Testing\n\nThe new tests ARE the deliverable; each is validated by mutation rather than by assertion of\na guess:\n\n- delete the `_is_at_level(...)` call from `_same_level_neighbors` → the direct\n  cross-level test goes red (verified: verdict flips False → True).\n- delete the `state is None` + tombstone stub branch → test (a) goes red (verified: `[]` →\n  `['tkt-target']`).\n- delete the `state[\"status\"] = tombstone_status` override → test (b) goes red (verified:\n  `['tkt-target']` → `[]`).\n- make `_read_tombstone_status`'s `except` return `None` instead of `\"deleted\"` → test (c)\n  goes red (verified: `['tkt-target']` → `[]`).\n\nEdge/negative coverage inside the new tests: an unreducible ticket dir, unparseable tombstone\nbytes, and a cross-level dep that must NOT be traversed. No new production behaviour, so\nthere is no happy path beyond the existing suite, which must stay green.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] `tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py` contains a test asserting\n      `check_cycle_at_level(\"task-M\", \"epic-B\", \"epic\", tracker) is False` for an\n      `epic-B depends_on task-M` tracker; checked by deleting the `_is_at_level` call from\n      `_same_level_neighbors` and observing that exact test fail, then reverting.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py` contains a test asserting\n      `check_cycle_at_level(\"epic-A\", \"epic-B\", \"epic\", tracker) is False` for an\n      `epic-B depends_on task-M depends_on epic-A` chain, so a lower-level hop cannot\n      reconnect two same-level nodes; checked by running that test against the unmodified\n      tree and seeing it pass.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py` contains a test that fails when the\n      `state is None` + tombstone-present stub branch of `_load_states_with_tombstones` is\n      deleted; checked by that deletion + `pytest` on the single test, then reverting.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py` contains a test that fails when the\n      `state[\"status\"] = tombstone_status` override is deleted; checked the same way.\n- [x] `tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py` contains a test that fails when\n      `_read_tombstone_status`'s exception handler stops returning `\"deleted\"`; checked the\n      same way.\n- [x] `git diff --name-only origin/main` lists only the two test files — no `src/rebar` path.\n- [x] `make lint` and `make typecheck` exit 0, and\n      `pytest tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py`\n      is green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"tests/scripts/graph/test_graph_cycles.py","reason":"characterization test for the cross-level traversal refusal"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_ticket_unblock.py","reason":"characterization tests for the tombstone loader branches"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07"],["relates_to","1841-d46c-87e4-4433"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2fe0-ce8b-4715-4e07","parent_status_uuid":"779c80b3-b96e-4979-85e9-e1ca19b3a0a4","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["remediation","tests","ae1b"],"ticket_id":"defc-658e-bfe1-4cab","ticket_type":"task","title":"Cover graph traversal seams surfaced by the loader/BFS refactor","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["774c19a6-4434-436f-a7a0-4708753fee27","7205fa08-6820-4fce-a01c-c7acb79778fd","6e90f20e-52e3-4bab-9b68-259610a1d577","2e3044c3-a6e0-42c0-a72a-5429eec9827f","2607c32f-a90e-4c95-bd14-8bb0ab696c99","3b559da3-4523-4e1b-b2eb-f2c1b53b8639","835c189a-a91d-4ed2-94ac-b84ca3992ea2","a2c16a96-4496-4b00-a919-30775fd0b3b8","657df098-65b8-420c-a9fe-e621cb3ae0b0","fdecc41b-5c84-45cc-88dc-c2ccea914dca","7b928bcd-049a-4f01-9c3d-e63f4a6f7366","e3219db2-aecf-492c-8cdc-ce9dc27a573e","b3a972d2-58ce-49a0-a328-d5541d817f94","d7a05347-6c07-401a-a8e2-38d91cc86fd5","91c1e532-4851-4d6b-ad2a-6f1b2f4512b8","edb78d20-7308-403d-babb-6e1c2688ccc2","779c80b3-b96e-4979-85e9-e1ca19b3a0a4","2f3e37db-af23-4d4e-8cb1-caad538994fb"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1786659682541651001,"uuid":"e73b97a8-635f-46ba-83ee-56cf2a16640f"}